Third-party notices
===================

Twenty-four laser starting points of the machining family (data/machining/*.json) are taken
from HobbyistLaserCalc, a calculator of settings for hobby lasers that is published under the
MIT licence (site: https://hobbyistlasercalc.com/, source:
https://github.com/SMSNYDER81/hobbyistlasercalc.com). Twelve are second figures of CO2 lasers
(the records marked "alternative": true, listed next to the main figure and never used for a
start); nine are diode points for thicknesses and woods that the main table does not have; three
are the only point of the new materials cherry, denim and mat board. Only numbers (power
setting, speed, passes, air assist) are used; no text, picture or page is. Each record names
the page it comes from in "source_info.url", and the speeds that the calculator gives in mm per
second are stored in mm per minute with the original value in "source_speed".

